1
00:00:00,505 --> 00:00:12,447
(Q11（单选）) As many of you here today have worked in the hotel industry for some time, I'm sure you have experienced the problem of high staff turnover in your hotels. 由于今天在座的很多人都在酒店行业工作了一段时间，我相信你们都经历过酒店员工流失率高的问题。⭐ staff turnover —— 员工流失率｜hotel industry —— 酒店行业｜experience a problem —— 经历/遇到某种问题

2
00:00:12,447 --> 00:00:22,095
Every hotel relies on having loyal and experienced members of staff who make sure that everything runs smoothly. 每家酒店都依赖忠诚且经验丰富的员工，确保一切运转顺利。⭐ rely on —— 依赖｜make sure (that) —— 确保｜run smoothly —— 顺利运转

3
00:00:22,095 --> 00:00:28,605
If staff are constantly changing, it can make life difficult for everyone. 如果员工不断更替，就会让所有人的工作变得困难。⭐ constantly —— 持续不断地｜make life difficult for —— 给……带来麻烦/增加困难

4
00:00:28,605 --> 00:00:33,538
But why do staff leave frequently in many hotels? 但为什么许多酒店的员工会频繁离职呢？⭐ leave —— 离职｜frequently —— 频繁地

5
00:00:33,538 --> 00:00:41,389
Of course, many hotel jobs, such as cleaning, are low-skilled and are not well-paid. 当然，许多酒店岗位，例如保洁工作，技术要求较低，而且薪资不高。⭐ low-skilled —— 技术要求低的｜well-paid —— 薪资优厚的（此处为否定）

6
00:00:41,389 --> 00:00:57,906
(Q11答案句) A lot of managers think it's this and the long hours that are the main causes of high staff turnover – but what they don't realise is that it's the lack of training in many hotel jobs which is a huge factor. 许多经理认为，低薪和长时间工作是员工流失率高的主要原因，但他们没有意识到，许多酒店岗位缺乏培训才是一个重要因素。⭐ long hours —— 长时间工作｜staff turnover —— 员工流失率｜lack of —— 缺乏｜a huge factor —— 一个重要因素｜realise —— 意识到

7
00:00:57,906 --> 00:01:03,300
(Q12) So, what kind of problems does a high turnover of staff cause? 那么，高员工流失率会带来哪些问题呢？⭐ turnover of staff —— 员工流失｜cause —— 导致，引发

8
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:16,050
(Q12答案句) Well, having to recruit new staff all the time can be very time-consuming, and managers may have to cover some duties while waiting for new staff to arrive. 不断招聘新员工会非常耗费时间，而且在等待新员工到岗期间，经理们可能还得承担部分工作职责。⭐ recruit —— 招聘｜time-consuming —— 耗时的｜cover some duties —— 临时承担工作职责

9
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:23,679
This means they don't have time to think about less immediate problems such as how to improve their service. 这意味着他们没有时间去思考那些不那么紧迫的问题，例如如何提升服务质量。⭐ less immediate —— 不那么紧迫的｜think about —— 考虑｜improve their service —— 提升服务质量

10
00:01:23,679 --> 00:01:30,633
When staff leave, it can also severely affect the colleagues they leave behind. 员工离职还会严重影响留下来的同事。⭐ severely affect —— 严重影响｜leave behind —— 留下

11
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:38,393
It has a negative effect on remaining staff, who may start to feel that they too should be thinking about leaving. 这会对留任员工产生负面影响，他们可能也会开始考虑离职。⭐ have a negative effect on —— 对……产生负面影响｜remaining staff —— 留任员工｜think about leaving —— 考虑离职

12
00:01:38,393 --> 00:01:42,062
(Q13) So, what can be done to change this situation? 那么，可以采取哪些措施来改变这种情况呢？⭐ what can be done —— 可以采取哪些措施｜change the situation —— 改变局面

13
00:01:42,062 --> 00:01:50,535
Firstly, managers should stop making basic errors which leave their staff feeling upset and resentful. 首先，管理者应该停止犯一些让员工感到沮丧和不满的基本错误。⭐ basic errors —— 基本错误｜leave somebody feeling… —— 使某人感到……｜resentful —— 愤愤不平的，心怀怨气的

14
00:01:50,535 --> 00:01:58,360
(Q13答案句) When organising shifts, for example, make sure you never give certain staff preferential treatment. 例如，在安排班次时，一定不要给予某些员工特殊优待。⭐ organise shifts —— 安排班次｜preferential treatment —— 特殊待遇，优待｜make sure —— 确保

15
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:07,911
All staff should be given some choice about when they work, and everyone should have to work some evening and weekend shifts. 所有员工都应该对自己的工作时间拥有一定选择权，而且每个人都应轮流上晚班和周末班。⭐ be given some choice —— 被赋予一定选择权｜shift —— 轮班，班次

16
00:02:07,911 --> 00:02:16,650
If you treat staff fairly, they'll be more likely to step in and help when extra staff are needed. 如果你公平对待员工，他们就更有可能在需要额外人手时主动帮忙。⭐ be more likely to —— 更有可能｜step in —— 主动介入，出手帮忙｜treat somebody fairly —— 公平对待某人

17
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:21,829
(Q14) Keeping staff happy has other tangible benefits for the business. 让员工保持满意还能为企业带来其他实实在在的好处。⭐ tangible benefits —— 实实在在的好处｜keep staff happy —— 让员工保持满意

18
00:02:21,829 --> 00:02:25,666
Take the Dunwich Hotel as an example. 以 Dunwich Hotel 为例。⭐ take … as an example —— 以……为例

19
00:02:25,666 --> 00:02:37,116
It had been experiencing a problem with staff complaints and in order to deal with this, invested in staff training and improved staff conditions. 该酒店一直面临员工投诉的问题，为了解决这一问题，它投资于员工培训，并改善了员工的工作条件。⭐ experience a problem with —— 遇到……方面的问题｜in order to —— 为了｜deal with —— 处理，应对｜invest in —— 投资于

20
00:02:37,116 --> 00:02:47,766
(Q14答案句) Not only did the level of complaints fall, but they also noticed a significant increase in the amount each customer spent during their stay. 不仅投诉数量下降了，他们还发现每位顾客在入住期间的消费金额显著增加。⭐ Not only did… but also… —— 不仅……而且……｜a significant increase in —— ……显著增长｜during their stay —— 在入住期间

21
00:02:47,766 --> 00:02:55,297
They have now introduced a customer loyalty scheme which is going really well. 如今，他们推出了一项顾客忠诚度计划，而且效果非常好。⭐ introduce a scheme —— 推出一项计划｜customer loyalty scheme —— 顾客忠诚度计划｜go well —— 进展顺利

22
00:02:55,297 --> 00:03:07,574
(Q15（配对）) Now I'd like to look at some ways you can reduce staff turnover in your hotels, and I'll do this by giving some examples of hotels where I've done some training recently. 现在我想介绍一些能够帮助你们降低酒店员工流失率的方法，我会结合一些我最近开展过培训的酒店案例来说明。⭐ look at —— 探讨，研究｜reduce staff turnover —— 降低员工流失率｜by doing… —— 通过……的方式｜give some examples of —— 举……的例子

23
00:03:07,574 --> 00:03:14,677
The Sun Club received feedback which showed that staff thought managers didn't value their opinions.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">Sun Club</span>收到了反馈，显示员工认为管理者并不重视他们的意见。 ⭐ receive feedback —— 收到反馈｜value somebody's opinions —— 重视某人的意见

24
00:03:14,677 --> 00:03:22,111
They weren't made to feel they were partners who were contributing to the success of the business as a whole. 员工没有感受到自己是企业的合作伙伴，也没有觉得自己正在为整个企业的成功作出贡献。⭐ be made to feel —— 被使得感到……｜contribute to —— 为……作出贡献｜as a whole —— 整体而言，从整体来看

25
00:03:22,111 --> 00:03:24,418
This situation has changed. 这种情况已经改变了。

26
00:03:24,418 --> 00:03:32,576
Junior staff at all levels are regularly invited to meetings where their ideas are welcomed. 各个层级的基层员工都会定期受邀参加会议，他们提出的想法也受到欢迎。⭐ at all levels —— 各个层级｜be invited to —— 被邀请参加｜be welcomed —— 受到欢迎/得到认可

27
00:03:32,576 --> 00:03:38,982
(Q16) A year ago, The Portland recognised the need to invest in staff retention. 一年前，The Portland 认识到了投资员工留任的重要性。⭐ recognise the need to… —— 意识到有必要……｜invest in —— 投资于｜staff retention —— 员工留任

28
00:03:38,982 --> 00:03:45,678
Their first step was to introduce a scheme for recognising talent amongst their employees. 他们采取的第一步措施，是推出一项识别员工人才的计划。⭐ introduce a scheme —— 推出一项计划｜recognise talent —— 发掘/识别人才｜amongst —— 在……之中（正式用法）

29
00:03:45,678 --> 00:03:55,702
The hope is that organising training for individuals with management potential will encourage them to stay with the business. 他们希望，为具有管理潜力的员工提供培训，能够鼓励他们继续留在公司。⭐ management potential —— 管理潜力｜encourage somebody to stay with… —— 鼓励某人继续留在……｜stay with the business —— 继续留在公司任职

30
00:03:55,702 --> 00:04:04,836
(Q17) At Bluewater, managers decided to recognise 50 high achievers from across the company's huge hotel chain. 在 Bluewater，管理层决定表彰来自整个酒店集团的50位优秀员工。⭐ high achiever —— 高绩效者，优秀员工｜from across… —— 来自整个……｜hotel chain —— 连锁酒店集团

31
00:04:04,836 --> 00:04:11,272
As a reward, they're sent on an all-expenses-paid trip abroad every year. 作为奖励，他们每年都会获得一次全程费用全包的海外旅行。⭐ as a reward —— 作为奖励｜all-expenses-paid —— 全程费用全包的｜be sent on a trip —— 被安排去旅行

32
00:04:11,272 --> 00:04:19,484
Fun is an important element in the trips, but there's also the opportunity to learn something useful. 旅行中娱乐是一个重要组成部分，但员工也有机会学到一些有用的东西。⭐ an important element —— 一个重要组成部分｜the opportunity to… —— ……的机会

33
00:04:19,484 --> 00:04:28,291
This year's trip included a visit to a brewery, where staff learned about the new beer that would be served in the hotel. 今年的旅行包括参观一家啤酒厂，员工在那里了解了酒店即将供应的新啤酒。⭐ include a visit to… —— 包括参观……｜brewery —— 啤酒厂｜learn about —— 了解

34
00:04:28,291 --> 00:04:35,353
(Q18) Pentlow Hotels identified that retention of junior reception staff was an issue.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">Pentlow Hotels</span>发现，前台初级员工的留任是一个问题。 ⭐ identify that… —— 发现/确认……｜retention —— 留任，保留｜be an issue —— 是一个问题

35
00:04:35,353 --> 00:04:46,245
In order to encourage them to see that working in a hotel could be worthwhile and rewarding, with good prospects, they introduced a management programme. 为了让他们认识到酒店工作是值得投入、富有成就感且具有良好发展前景的，酒店推出了一项管理培训项目。⭐ in order to —— 为了｜worthwhile and rewarding —— 值得投入且有成就感的｜good prospects —— 良好的发展前景｜management programme —— 管理培训项目

36
00:04:46,245 --> 00:04:54,418
These staff were given additional responsibilities and the chance to work in various roles in the hotel. 这些员工被赋予了更多职责，并获得了在酒店不同岗位工作的机会。⭐ additional responsibilities —— 更多职责｜various roles —— 不同岗位｜be given the chance to… —— 获得……的机会

37
00:04:54,418 --> 00:04:58,977
(Q19) Green Planet wanted to be seen as a caring employer.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">Green Planet</span>希望被视为一家关爱员工的雇主。 ⭐ be seen as —— 被视为｜caring employer —— 关爱员工的雇主

38
00:04:58,977 --> 00:05:10,744
To make life easier for staff, many of whom had childcare responsibilities, the hotel began issuing vouchers to help cover the cost of childcare. 为了让员工生活更加便利，考虑到其中许多人需要照顾孩子，酒店开始发放代金券，以帮助承担托儿费用。⭐ make life easier for —— 让……生活更轻松｜childcare responsibilities —— 育儿责任｜issue vouchers —— 发放代金券｜cover the cost of —— 支付/承担……的费用

39
00:05:10,744 --> 00:05:17,543
(Q20) Louise Marsh at The Amesbury has one of the best staff retention rates in the business.&nbsp; <span style="color: oklch(0.278 0.033 256.848);">Amesbury</span>酒店的 Louise Marsh 创造了业内最优秀的员工留任率之一。 ⭐ staff retention rate —— 员工留任率｜in the business —— 在业内

40
00:05:17,543 --> 00:05:26,623
Since she joined the company, she has made a huge effort to achieve this by creating a co-operative and supportive environment. 自加入公司以来，她一直付出巨大努力，通过营造合作互助、彼此支持的工作环境来实现这一目标。⭐ make a huge effort —— 作出巨大努力｜achieve this by… —— 通过……实现这一目标｜co-operative and supportive environment —— 合作互助、支持性的环境

41
00:05:26,623 --> 00:05:31,904
For her, the staff are part of a large family where everyone is valued. 在她看来，员工就是一个大家庭的一部分，每个人都受到重视。⭐ be part of —— 是……的一部分｜be valued —— 被重视

42
00:05:31,904 --> 00:05:34,404
OK, now I'd like to … 好的，现在我想……⭐ I'd like to… —— 我想……（正式演讲中的过渡表达）

